name 'building-data-driven-systems-preassessment-q4_2025'

question 'When using the `.map()` method to display an array of data on a webpage, what is its primary role?'

wrong 'To filter out data that the user doesn\'t want to see.'
wrong 'To permanently delete items from the original array after they are shown.'
right 'To iterate through the array and return a new set of elements, such as HTML tags, for each item.'
wrong 'To sort the array alphabetically before it is sent to the DOM.'

allow_multiple_attempts false

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 2

`.map()` is a transformation tool. It takes an array of data and "maps" each item to a new structure, typically HTML elements like `<li>` or `<div>`, without changing the original data. 
MARKDOWN
